     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\">Given the following df:<div><br></div><div style=\"border:1px solid rgb(187,187,187);word-wrap:break-word;background-color:rgb(250,250,250)\"><code><div><span style=\"color:#000\">df </span><span style=\"color:#660\">&lt;-</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> data</span><span style=\"color:#660\">.</span><span style=\"color:#000\">frame</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">lat </span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> c</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#066\">36.1</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#066\">36</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#066\">36</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#066\">36.1</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#066\">36.1</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#066\">36</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#066\">36</span><span style=\"color:#660\">),</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> lng </span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> c</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(-</span><span style=\"color:#066\">94.17</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#660\">-</span><span style=\"color:#066\">94.2</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#660\">-</span><span style=\"color:#066\">94.14</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#660\">-</span><span style=\"color:#066\">94.2</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#660\">-</span><span style=\"color:#066\">94.14</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#660\">-</span><span style=\"color:#066\">94.14</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#660\">-</span><span style=\"color:#066\">94.2</span><span style=\"color:#660\">),</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> shape </span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> c</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#080\">&quot;triangle&quot;</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#080\">&quot;triangle&quot;</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#080\">&quot;triangle&quot;</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#080\">&quot;square&quot;</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#080\">&quot;square&quot;</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#080\">&quot;square&quot;</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#080\">&quot;square&quot;</span><span style=\"color:#660\">))</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br><br><br></span><span style=\"color:#660\">&gt;</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> df<br>   lat    lng    shape<br></span><span style=\"color:#066\">1</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#066\">36.1</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#660\">-</span><span style=\"color:#066\">94.17</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> triangle<br></span><span style=\"color:#066\">2</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#066\">36.0</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#660\">-</span><span style=\"color:#066\">94.20</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> triangle<br></span><span style=\"color:#066\">3</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#066\">36.0</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#660\">-</span><span style=\"color:#066\">94.14</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> triangle<br></span><span style=\"color:#066\">4</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#066\">36.1</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#660\">-</span><span style=\"color:#066\">94.20</span><span style=\"color:#000\">   square<br></span><span style=\"color:#066\">5</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#066\">36.1</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#660\">-</span><span style=\"color:#066\">94.14</span><span style=\"color:#000\">   square<br></span><span style=\"color:#066\">6</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#066\">36.0</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#660\">-</span><span style=\"color:#066\">94.14</span><span style=\"color:#000\">   square<br></span><span style=\"color:#066\">7</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#066\">36.0</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#660\">-</span><span style=\"color:#066\">94.20</span><span style=\"color:#000\">   square</span></div></code></div><div><div><br></div></div><div><br></div><div>suppose I want to overlay the df shapes onto a leaflet map via addPolygons().  Either of the following work well:</div><div><br></div><div style=\"border:1px solid rgb(187,187,187);word-wrap:break-word;background-color:rgb(250,250,250)\"><code><div><span style=\"color:#000\">df </span><span style=\"color:#660\">%&gt;%</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> filter</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">shape </span><span style=\"color:#660\">==</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#080\">&quot;triangle&quot;</span><span style=\"color:#660\">)</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#660\">%&gt;%</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> leaflet</span><span style=\"color:#660\">()</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#660\">%&gt;%</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> addPolygons</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">lat </span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#660\">~</span><span style=\"color:#000\">lat</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> lng </span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#660\">~</span><span style=\"color:#000\">lng</span><span style=\"color:#660\">)</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br><br><br><br><br>df </span><span style=\"color:#660\">%&gt;%</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> filter</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">shape </span><span style=\"color:#660\">==</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#080\">&quot;square&quot;</span><span style=\"color:#660\">)</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#660\">%&gt;%</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> leaflet</span><span style=\"color:#660\">()</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#660\">%&gt;%</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> addPolygons</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">lat </span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#660\">~</span><span style=\"color:#000\">lat</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> lng </span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#660\">~</span><span style=\"color:#000\">lng</span><span style=\"color:#660\">)</span></div></code></div><div><br><br></div><div><br></div><div><br></div><div>If, however, the order of that lat/lng arguments aren&#39;t just so (ensured by subsetting via filter() above), you get erratic plotting, eg:</div><div><br><div style=\"border:1px solid rgb(187,187,187);word-wrap:break-word;background-color:rgb(250,250,250)\"><code><div><span style=\"color:#000\">df </span><span style=\"color:#660\">%&gt;%</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> leaflet</span><span style=\"color:#660\">()</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#660\">%&gt;%</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> addPolygons</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">lat </span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#660\">~</span><span style=\"color:#000\">lat</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> lng </span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#660\">~</span><span style=\"color:#000\">lng</span><span style=\"color:#660\">)</span></div></code></div><br><br></div><div><br></div><div>How can I solve this?</div><div><br></div><div>The bigger picture is that I have a much larger df for which I want to have a user select regions in a shiny app, but I need each region plotted discreetly, regardless of how many or which are selected.</div><div><br></div><div>Thanks in advance.</div><div><br></div></div>"
